      'Outbound Egypt files fail when families treat HBE or SSH as automatic import stations because those codes appear in the seed. A Sharm holiday ticket against a Cairo-named GOVS permission is a refusal at the wrong apron. The next fail is starting with a MOCCAE import permit, which cannot export an animal, or pasting inbound “sample within 90 days before travel” titer language onto an Egyptian arrival that may instead want GOVS-specific tests or an on-arrival inspection. Quarantine uncertainty is the Africa-family difficulty: circulars change, inspection rooms close, and a crate that would have released at Hamad or Muscat can sit. Certificate maths collide when the UAE export window is opened before GOVS names a date, then a Cairo cargo slot slips. EgyptAir cabin-or-cargo seed language from an inbound memory does not prove cabin from Dubai. Emirates and Etihad stay cargo in the seed. A JLT owner who books Sharm because the passenger fare is cheaper, against a Cairo-named GOVS permission, will meet the crate at the wrong apron. Do not invent GOVS, quarantine or airline fee numerals. Quote via Get Route Checked or WhatsApp +971504782999.',
    howItWorks:
      'Scenario: a dog leaving JLT for a New Cairo compound, owner flying EgyptAir the same night and refusing a Sharm connection because GOVS inspection is expected at CAI. Month −3: read the current GOVS import / veterinary-quarantine instruction, confirm whether an advance permit or notification is required from the UAE, and name Cairo International on that permission. Do not open a UAE import-permit application. Month −2 to −1: once Egyptian dates exist, request the MOCCAE export health certificate so its validity window (commonly 30 days from issue — verify on the portal) still covers departure from DXB, DWC or AUH. In parallel, confirm live-animal acceptance: EgyptAir cabin-or-cargo, Emirates cargo, Etihad cargo — all unverified. Refuse an HBE or SSH rewrite unless GOVS and the carrier confirm import handling. Week −1: crate check for a longer sector than a GCC hop, parasite treatments if GOVS or the airline requires them, and a Cairo inspection-room collection brief — not a DXB cargo-village story and not a “we will collect in Sharm and drive to Maadi.” Arrival day is a GOVS / veterinary-quarantine story at the named Egyptian airport. This timeline is a planning narrative, not a guaranteed duration.',
    airportsNarrative:
      'Egyptian arrival gateways on the seed are Cairo (CAI), Alexandria / Borg El Arab (HBE) and Sharm el-Sheikh (SSH). CAI is the working default for international pet inspection. HBE and SSH are seed cities, not automatic import stations — do not assume a North Coast or Red Sea field can release a consignment just because the code appears in the table. The GOVS permission and the air waybill must name the same airport. UAE departure side: Dubai International (DXB) is common for the passenger ticket even when the pet moves as cargo or hold depending on the outbound product. Al Maktoum / Dubai World Central (DWC) is cargo-centric on many SkyCargo-style consignments. Abu Dhabi (AUH) applies when Etihad routing is used — confirm the live pet product toward the named Egyptian city. Write the same IATA on the GOVS permission, the UAE export certificate and the AWB. New Cairo and Maadi collection should still assume Cairo inspection unless GOVS names another port in writing. A Sharm or Alexandria rewrite against a Cairo-named GOVS permission is how crates sit on the wrong apron. This three-airport destination map is an Africa-family inspection story, not a GCC single-runway neighbour hop.',
    airlinesNarrative:
      'Seed airlines outbound are EgyptAir (cabin-or-cargo), Emirates (cargo) and Etihad (cargo). From Dubai, re-confirm each product for the UAE→Egypt city pair; inbound Cairo acceptance does not transfer. EgyptAir’s cabin-or-cargo seed is not a cabin promise leaving DXB. Emirates stays cargo. Etihad stays cargo; any AUH cabin language is OD-specific and belongs on /guides/etihad-pet-policy/, not on this GOVS corridor page. For a UAE chooser see /guides/pet-flight-options-dubai/. A JLT passenger departing the same night still needs a confirmed live-animal product toward the GOVS-named airport, usually CAI. Confirm EgyptAir for the UAE→CAI pair first; treat Emirates and Etihad as cargo unless a first-party check updates the row. Inbound Cairo cabin-or-cargo language does not transfer to a Dubai departure, and a Sharm holiday ticket is not a GOVS inspection plan. Confirm the live EgyptAir page for the exact UAE→CAI pair before anyone pays for a crate. We do not add Jazeera, Gulf Air or Oman Air to this Africa-family block. All rows stay unverified. PetClear claims no airline affiliation and never claims a ministry endorsement of any carrier. Quote-only via Get Route Checked or WhatsApp +971504782999 after GOVS names the inspection airport.',
